%% Rate-limit token bucket — per Profile
%% Source: spec/22-git-logs-v2/10-rate-limit-and-payload.md

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CI as CI/CD Caller
    participant API as REST Controller
    participant RL as RateLimiter
    participant TR as WP Transient (gitlogs_rate_{ProfileId})
    participant SVC as LogIngestService
    participant AUD as AuditTrail

    CI->>API: POST /append-log (TempToken, body)
    API->>API: Resolve Profile from TempToken
    API->>RL: check(ProfileId)
    RL->>TR: read { Tokens, LastRefillAt }
    TR-->>RL: { Tokens=0.4, LastRefillAt=t0 }
    RL->>RL: refill: Tokens = min(cap, Tokens + (now-t0)*rate)

    alt Tokens >= 1
        RL->>TR: write { Tokens-1, now }
        RL-->>API: allow
        API->>SVC: ingest(body)
        SVC-->>API: ack
        API-->>CI: 200 OK + Retrieval hints
    else Tokens < 1
        RL-->>API: deny, retryAfter = ceil((1-Tokens)/rate)
        API->>AUD: log(LogPush, Outcome=Rejected, Detail=rate)
        API-->>CI: 429 + Retry-After header
    end
